  "_mutation_equivalence": "The seven surviving mutants are equivalent. lea ecx,[esp-8] -> esp-9/esp-7 and the mask 0xfffffff8 -> 0xfffffff9/0xfffffff7 only move the 8-byte scratch slot inside the function's own 0x10-byte frame (ESP is dword-aligned at entry), which nobody else reads. add ecx,0x7fffffff -> 0x7ffffffe (both paths) differs only when the f32 rounding error x-r is +/-1.4e-45 (bits 0x00000001 / 0x80000001), and -> 0x80000000 only when it is -0.0 (0x80000000): the fraction path runs only when the rounded value r is nonzero, so |x| >= 0.5 and a nonzero error is at least 2^-64 (an f32 normal), and x - r is +0.0, never -0.0, when they are equal under round-to-nearest.",
